In the checked `e2e-playwright-tests` workflow, the setup only runs `npm ci` before `npx playwright test`; this newly introduced `page` fixture launches Chromium, but Playwright 1.62 does not install its browser binary during package installation. On a clean `ubuntu-latest` runner the job therefore exits with an “executable doesn't exist” error before this test runs. Playwright's [official CI example](https://playwright.dev/docs/ci-intro) runs `npx playwright install --with-deps` after `npm ci`; add that step or use the official Playwright container.

AGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L263-L266](https://github.com/scottdensmore/PetSpotR/blob/a7a5d4e19bf07c61fbff83f6e82ae50080ab8d3b/AGENTS.md#L263-L266)

